    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0437" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg387"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Dun.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information, in
                    connection with your No. 48, of December 23, 1893, and the Department’s No. 47,
                    of February 19 last, copy of a dispatch, No. 88, of the 5th ultimo, from the
                    consul of the United States at Nagasaki, and of the Department’s reply, No. 28,
                    of the 22d instant, in relation to the case of George W. Lake.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>





